# Nimpass frontend — PRODUCTION (Nimiq Mainnet)
#
# Everything prefixed with VITE_ is inlined into the public bundle and is
# readable by anyone who opens the page. No secret, key, seed phrase or private
# RPC credential belongs in this file or in any VITE_ variable
# (docs/09-SECURITY.md §27-§30). The backend owns the RPC endpoint; the
# frontend never talks to a Nimiq node directly.
#
# The development/Testnet counterpart is `.env.example`.

# --- Environment and network ------------------------------------------------
#
# Both are mandatory and are validated against each other at build time by
# `config/deployment.ts`, which the Vite config calls before it builds
# anything: `production` requires `MAINNET`. A build with the wrong pair fails
# rather than shipping.
#
# This declares which network *Nimpass* is configured for. It is not, and can
# never be, proof of which chain a transaction belongs to — Nimiq Pay picks its
# own network, and its hidden developer menu can force either one. The backend
# re-derives the network of every transaction from the chain itself and rejects
# a cross-network payment outright (docs/04-NIMIQ-MINI-APPS.md §49).
VITE_APP_ENV=production
VITE_NIMIQ_NETWORK=MAINNET

# --- Backend ----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Same-origin `/api` is the recommended shape, and the one `vercel.json`
# implements: the session cookie stays first-party, which matters inside the
# Nimiq Pay WebView, where a cross-origin API host makes the session a
# cross-origin cookie the WebView is free to drop.
#
# An absolute HTTPS origin works too, provided the backend's PUBLIC_ORIGIN and
# CORS allow this exact origin and the two are on the same site.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/

# --- Fixtures ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Off, and structurally unable to be on: the fixture layer is behind
# `import.meta.env.DEV` and is eliminated from production builds, which
# `src/dev/production-isolation.test.ts` verifies against the built artefact.
VITE_DEV_FIXTURES=0

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Milliseconds to wait for Nimiq Pay to inject the provider before concluding
# this is an ordinary browser and falling through to the Nimiq Hub. Defaults to
# 3000.
# VITE_NIMIQ_INIT_TIMEOUT_MS=3000

# The Nimiq Hub endpoint is NOT configurable on Mainnet, by design. It follows
# the network — https://hub.nimiq.com — and `VITE_NIMIQ_HUB_URL` is ignored
# when VITE_NIMIQ_NETWORK=MAINNET, so a misconfigured build cannot route real
# payments through an arbitrary origin (docs/09-SECURITY.md §101).
#
# The Hub is the ordinary-browser fallback only. Inside Nimiq Pay, Nimpass uses
# the injected Nimiq provider through @nimiq/mini-app-sdk and never the Hub.

# Canonical origin for cross-device purchase links. Defaults to the current
# HTTPS origin, which is normally correct in production.
# VITE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://app.example.com
